      ],
      "text": "**If you mean this morning, I’d skip the outdoor walk today, October 17.** Singapore’s official forecast put the 24-hour PSI at **150–230**—unhealthy to very unhealthy. NEA advises older adults to minimize prolonged or strenuous outdoor exertion when the PSI is unhealthy, and to minimize outdoor activity when it is very unhealthy. ([weather.gov.sg](https://www.weather.gov.sg/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026/))\n\nAn easy indoor walk or gentle movement at home would be a safer substitute. For any outdoor activity, check the latest **1-hour PM2.5** for her area in myENV first; Singapore’s Meteorological Service says to use that reading for immediate plans. If she has heart or lung disease, be especially cautious. ([weather.gov.sg](https://www.weather.gov.sg/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026/))",
